WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.150
Common birds, like
the pigeon shown here,

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:05.850
exhibit grace and
precision in flight

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:09.510
that far exceeds our best
robotic capabilities.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:11.820
Inspired by these
maneuvers, we have

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:15.360
built an autonomous
aircraft capable of fast,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.250
accurate, and repeatable flight.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.700
Utilizing motion capture
for feedback control,

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.830
we demonstrate this
system by flying

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.605
through a gap that is smaller
than the aircraft's wingspan.

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:37.450
Accurate control in
these flight regimes

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:40.840
is difficult because of
the complex airflow induced

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.200
at high angles of attack.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.790
We capture 120 frames per
second onboard video for use

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.470
in studying machine vision.

00:00:50.470 --> 00:00:54.310
Here, we demonstrate avoiding
vertical and horizontal

00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:55.030
obstacles.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.940
Finally, we show these
videos in real-time.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:05.690
[WHIRRING]

